{:edb/db-before-t 2767 :edb/db-after-t 2768 :edb/tx-data [[13194139536080 50 #inst "2026-10-09T14:32:49.484Z" 13194139536080 true] [17592186124521 1020 #edb/ref 17592186382651 13194139536080 true] [17592186124522 1020 #edb/ref 17592186382658 13194139536080 true] [17592186382651 1017 #edb/ref 17592186382652 13194139536080 true] [17592186382651 1089 "q-140045" 13194139536080 true] [17592186382651 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536080 true] [17592186382651 1100 "Consider the following matrices:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 6 & 7\\end{aligned}],\\,D=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,P=[\\begin{aligned}∗ & 1 \\\\ ∗ & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nGiven that $A=PD{P}^{-1},$ find the first column of the matrix $P.$" 13194139536080 true] [17592186382651 1113 #uuid "16966b44-d262-59a2-bf48-8567403d396f" 13194139536080 true] [17592186382651 1145 "From the diagonal matrix $D=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]$, we deduce that the eigenvalues of the matrix $A$ are ${\\lambda }_{1}=3$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=4.$\n\nSo, the first column of $P$ corresponds to the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=3.$ \n\nNow, we simply need to find an eigenvector that corresponds to ${\\lambda }_{1}=3.$ Computing $A-3I,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-3I & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 6 & 7\\end{aligned}]-3[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ 6 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations with the augmented matrix $M$ which we reduce to its row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we obtain ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{2}{3}{x}_{2}.$ Hence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{3}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting ${x}_{2}=3,$ we get the eigenvector \n\n$$\n{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, $P=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139536080 true] [17592186382652 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382653 13194139536080 true] [17592186382652 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382654 13194139536080 true] [17592186382652 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382655 13194139536080 true] [17592186382652 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382656 13194139536080 true] [17592186382652 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382657 13194139536080 true] [17592186382652 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536080 true] [17592186382652 1041 "selection" 13194139536080 true] [17592186382652 1104 #edb/ref 17592186382657 13194139536080 true] [17592186382652 1110 #uuid "484e247f-cdf6-58ee-b821-37819ce89d49" 13194139536080 true] [17592186382653 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139536080 true] [17592186382653 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536080 true] [17592186382653 1111 #uuid "9c2c83b5-ac91-57a3-ac6c-76f0fbbdbbe7" 13194139536080 true] [17592186382654 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" 13194139536080 true] [17592186382654 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536080 true] [17592186382654 1111 #uuid "28850b83-c4b0-57bb-8209-a7274e569b86" 13194139536080 true] [17592186382655 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" 13194139536080 true] [17592186382655 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536080 true] [17592186382655 1111 #uuid "a850083c-117b-59f3-ba15-6d5a442d2621" 13194139536080 true] [17592186382656 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" 13194139536080 true] [17592186382656 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536080 true] [17592186382656 1111 #uuid "e93a9c55-8fec-550d-808f-afd03f26d3cc" 13194139536080 true] [17592186382657 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" 13194139536080 true] [17592186382657 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536080 true] [17592186382657 1111 #uuid "b9f5a770-68f5-5722-8f61-48518553a391" 13194139536080 true] [17592186382658 1017 #edb/ref 17592186382659 13194139536080 true] [17592186382658 1089 "q-37633" 13194139536080 true] [17592186382658 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536080 true] [17592186382658 1100 "Given the matrix \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{aligned}]$,\nfind a diagonal matrix $D$ and an invertible matrix $P$ such that $D={P}^{-1}BP.$" 13194139536080 true] [17592186382658 1113 #uuid "a4b19937-90d1-5717-b7a0-7b53ad9d3dcb" 13194139536080 true] [17592186382658 1145 "We apply the diagonalization algorithm.\n\n**Step 1.**  We need to find the eigenvalues of the matrix. Since matrix $A$ is triangular, its eigenvalues are the entries on the main diagonal: \n\n$\\,$ ${\\lambda }_{1}=7\\,$ and $\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=-5$\n\n**Step 2.** Now, we need to find an eigenvector basis of $B.$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=7,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B-7I & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{aligned}]-7[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -12\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations with the augmented matrix $M$ which we reduce to its row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -12 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has one pivot column (the $2$nd one). Thus, ${x}_{1}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we obtain ${x}_{2}=0.$ Hence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{1}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting ${x}_{1}=1,$ we get the eigenvector ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=-5,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B-(-5)I & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{aligned}]+5[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}12 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a homogeneous system of linear equations with the matrix as above. Note, the matrix is already in row echelon form. There is one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we obtain ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{1}{3}{x}_{2}.$ Hence, the general solution is \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{3}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting ${x}_{2}=3,$ we get the eigenvector ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Step 3.** We construct the diagonal matrix $D$ and the invertible matrix $P$ as follows:\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{aligned}],\\,P=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139536080 true] [17592186382659 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382660 13194139536080 true] [17592186382659 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382661 13194139536080 true] [17592186382659 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382662 13194139536080 true] [17592186382659 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382663 13194139536080 true] [17592186382659 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382664 13194139536080 true] [17592186382659 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536080 true] [17592186382659 1041 "selection" 13194139536080 true] [17592186382659 1104 #edb/ref 17592186382662 13194139536080 true] [17592186382659 1110 #uuid "6e607a58-c096-5640-8687-a2892d9455d5" 13194139536080 true] [17592186382660 1034 "$D=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{aligned}]$ and $P=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]$" 13194139536080 true] [17592186382660 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536080 true] [17592186382660 1111 #uuid "ba32fd11-6da9-501e-a2d9-85de306160b8" 13194139536080 true] [17592186382661 1034 "$B$ is not diagonalizable" 13194139536080 true] [17592186382661 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536080 true] [17592186382661 1111 #uuid "4feddca6-5376-5c7a-a476-c66a930662bc" 13194139536